{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["For you went up onto your father's bed — and so it is written in Chronicles: ״וּבְחַלְּלוֹ יְצוּעֵי אָבִיו נָתַן בְּכֹרָתוֹ לִבְנֵי יוֹסֵף בֶּן יִשְׂרָאֵל וְלֹא לְהִתְיַחֵשׂ לַבְּכֹרָה כִּי יְהוּדָה גָּבַר בְּאֶחָיו וְלְנָגִיד מִמֶּנּוּ וְהַבְּכֹרָה לְיוֹסֵף״." "He went up onto my couch — that is, my couch was going up. Many verb forms (לשון פעל) are interpreted as noun forms (לשון פועל), as in: ״נָתַתִּי כֶּסֶף הַשָּׂדֶה״ — 'I am giving.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:40.618017136Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}